1
00:00:00,433 --> 00:00:02,000
Many people like Su Dongpo

2
00:00:02,066 --> 00:00:03,466
but the easiest mistake we make

3
00:00:03,566 --> 00:00:05,666
is treating him as a born optimist

4
00:00:05,833 --> 00:00:07,200
as if being demoted

5
00:00:07,233 --> 00:00:08,400
just meant eating something good

6
00:00:08,433 --> 00:00:09,366
writing a few poems

7
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:10,200
smiling it off

8
00:00:10,233 --> 00:00:11,500
and life moves on

9
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:12,566
So people say

10
00:00:12,666 --> 00:00:14,100
Su Dongpo had such a great mindset

11
00:00:14,166 --> 00:00:16,266
if only I could be half as open as him

12
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:17,233
But I think

13
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,000
what's truly powerful about Su Dongpo

14
00:00:19,033 --> 00:00:20,366
isn't that he was born a positive thinker

15
00:00:20,466 --> 00:00:22,033
but that he never pinned his entire life

16
00:00:22,066 --> 00:00:23,500
on a single identity

17
00:00:23,566 --> 00:00:25,100
This goes against common sense

18
00:00:25,133 --> 00:00:27,033
we assume resilience comes from mindset

19
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:28,166
but often

20
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:29,466
it comes from structure

21
00:00:29,533 --> 00:00:31,266
If a person has only one identity

22
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:32,766
the moment it's taken away

23
00:00:32,766 --> 00:00:33,600
they collapse

24
00:00:33,733 --> 00:00:36,500
But if they have many places to anchor themselves

25
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,766
even when pushed down on one side

26
00:00:37,866 --> 00:00:39,700
they can still rise from another

27
00:00:39,700 --> 00:00:42,066
This video doesn't turn Su Dongpo into chicken soup

28
00:00:42,166 --> 00:00:44,233
or tell you to laugh everything off

29
00:00:44,333 --> 00:00:46,266
just one idea an ordinary person can use

30
00:00:46,366 --> 00:00:47,733
the steadiest state in life

31
00:00:47,733 --> 00:00:48,866
isn't never falling

32
00:00:48,933 --> 00:00:51,366
it's not letting yourself lean on just one support

33
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:53,066
Picture this

34
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:55,000
you've been at a company for years

35
00:00:55,133 --> 00:00:56,366
your title is on the card

36
00:00:56,433 --> 00:00:57,800
people in the group chat call you teacher

37
00:00:57,933 --> 00:00:58,733
relatives mention you

38
00:00:58,733 --> 00:01:00,166
and say you're at a big company

39
00:01:00,366 --> 00:01:01,500
At first you know

40
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:02,466
this is just work

41
00:01:02,666 --> 00:01:03,700
but over time

42
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:05,233
you slowly turn it into who you are

43
00:01:05,433 --> 00:01:06,300
Then one day

44
00:01:06,333 --> 00:01:07,200
the department reshuffles

45
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:08,166
your role changes

46
00:01:08,233 --> 00:01:09,533
you're moved off the core project

47
00:01:09,533 --> 00:01:10,633
or you lose your job entirely

48
00:01:10,666 --> 00:01:11,366
The hardest part

49
00:01:11,366 --> 00:01:12,766
isn't the drop in income

50
00:01:12,766 --> 00:01:14,566
it's that you suddenly don't know who you are

51
00:01:14,666 --> 00:01:15,766
your phone goes quiet

52
00:01:15,766 --> 00:01:17,000
meetings happen without you

53
00:01:17,033 --> 00:01:18,333
people stop asking your opinion

54
00:01:18,333 --> 00:01:19,100
and you realize

55
00:01:19,166 --> 00:01:20,333
that much of your confidence

56
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:21,566
was never grown in you

57
00:01:21,566 --> 00:01:22,866
it was hanging on that seat

58
00:01:22,933 --> 00:01:24,600
Su Dongpo was demoted many times in his life

59
00:01:24,666 --> 00:01:25,900
from court to province

60
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:27,200
from the center to the edges

61
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:28,366
of course he hurt

62
00:01:28,366 --> 00:01:29,266
he felt wronged

63
00:01:29,366 --> 00:01:30,866
he felt fate was unfair

64
00:01:31,033 --> 00:01:32,000
he wasn't made of stone

65
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:33,433
but he never fully broke

66
00:01:33,533 --> 00:01:35,066
because he was never just an official

67
00:01:35,166 --> 00:01:36,300
he was also a writer

68
00:01:36,300 --> 00:01:37,033
a friend

69
00:01:37,066 --> 00:01:37,866
a cook

70
00:01:37,866 --> 00:01:38,866
a traveler

71
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:40,900
someone who could taste a coarse meal

72
00:01:41,033 --> 00:01:42,533
and someone who could find new words

73
00:01:42,533 --> 00:01:44,000
in the worst situations

74
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:45,366
This isn't simple optimism

75
00:01:45,433 --> 00:01:47,800
it's his life not being kept in one basket

76
00:01:47,866 --> 00:01:48,700
the title fell

77
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:49,800
his words remained

78
00:01:49,866 --> 00:01:50,700
the place turned cold

79
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:51,800
his appetite remained

80
00:01:51,866 --> 00:01:52,766
people grew distant

81
00:01:52,766 --> 00:01:54,666
his ability to joke about the world remained

82
00:01:54,866 --> 00:01:56,066
With these things

83
00:01:56,133 --> 00:01:58,100
a person can't be fully pierced by one lost role

84
00:01:58,533 --> 00:02:00,466
We say Su Dongpo was broad-minded

85
00:02:00,633 --> 00:02:01,866
but that word open

86
00:02:01,933 --> 00:02:03,200
is too easy to say lightly

87
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:04,933
as if you just think positively

88
00:02:04,933 --> 00:02:06,200
and things won't feel so heavy

89
00:02:06,466 --> 00:02:07,833
But reality doesn't work that way

90
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:08,966
rent is still due

91
00:02:09,100 --> 00:02:10,166
parents still worry

92
00:02:10,266 --> 00:02:11,266
kids still cost money

93
00:02:11,333 --> 00:02:12,266
when work goes wrong

94
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:13,800
people still judge you

95
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:14,866
just cheer up

96
00:02:14,866 --> 00:02:16,033
doesn't fix any of this

97
00:02:16,333 --> 00:02:17,500
Su Dongpo's strength

98
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:19,266
isn't naming bad things as good

99
00:02:19,466 --> 00:02:21,066
it's that after the bad thing hits

100
00:02:21,133 --> 00:02:22,666
he could still find other supports

101
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:24,266
Writing is a support

102
00:02:24,333 --> 00:02:25,500
today you were rejected

103
00:02:25,533 --> 00:02:27,266
but you can still write down how you feel

104
00:02:27,266 --> 00:02:28,833
and you're not fully swallowed

105
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:30,466
Cooking is a support

106
00:02:30,533 --> 00:02:33,266
if someone can still invent a little joy in a meal

107
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:35,366
life doesn't all become drudgery

108
00:02:35,666 --> 00:02:36,900
Friends are a support

109
00:02:36,966 --> 00:02:38,600
if someone still wants to hear you

110
00:02:38,633 --> 00:02:40,566
you know you're more than a job title

111
00:02:40,733 --> 00:02:42,100
Humor is a support too

112
00:02:42,133 --> 00:02:43,266
when you can still smile

113
00:02:43,366 --> 00:02:44,900
not because it isn't serious

114
00:02:44,933 --> 00:02:47,666
but because you haven't given fate the final word

115
00:02:47,866 --> 00:02:49,033
it sounds small

116
00:02:49,066 --> 00:02:50,100
but it carries weight

117
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:51,666
Many modern people break down

118
00:02:51,733 --> 00:02:54,033
not because the blow really is too much

119
00:02:54,133 --> 00:02:56,000
but because their life runs on one track

120
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:56,933
in school

121
00:02:56,933 --> 00:02:57,866
only grades

122
00:02:57,933 --> 00:02:58,733
at work

123
00:02:58,733 --> 00:02:59,633
only titles

124
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:00,633
after marriage

125
00:03:00,633 --> 00:03:01,833
only family judgment

126
00:03:01,966 --> 00:03:02,933
after starting an account

127
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:04,166
only view counts

128
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:06,466
each stage hands the whole self to one metric

129
00:03:06,633 --> 00:03:07,433
metric looks good

130
00:03:07,433 --> 00:03:08,400
the whole person lights up

131
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:09,300
metric looks bad

132
00:03:09,333 --> 00:03:10,300
the whole person dims

133
00:03:10,433 --> 00:03:11,466
this is dangerous

134
00:03:11,533 --> 00:03:13,833
because the world won't always hand you good metrics

135
00:03:14,033 --> 00:03:15,300
someone truly antifragile

136
00:03:15,333 --> 00:03:16,900
isn't someone whose metrics always look good

137
00:03:16,933 --> 00:03:18,266
it's someone whose metrics look bad

138
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:20,166
and still has other corners to breathe in

139
00:03:20,566 --> 00:03:22,666
I want to use a very everyday phrase

140
00:03:22,966 --> 00:03:25,400
ordinary people need their own emotional cash flow

141
00:03:25,466 --> 00:03:26,900
what's emotional cash flow

142
00:03:27,066 --> 00:03:28,900
the things that may not make you rich

143
00:03:28,933 --> 00:03:30,800
but keep refilling you

144
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:32,966
like a route you can walk

145
00:03:33,033 --> 00:03:34,766
one or two people you can be real with

146
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,966
a hobby you don't have to compete at

147
00:03:37,066 --> 00:03:39,033
a skill you can slowly get better at

148
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:41,066
a cheap but steady kind of joy

149
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:43,966
these look less useful than a promotion

150
00:03:44,066 --> 00:03:45,766
but in your low moments

151
00:03:45,766 --> 00:03:47,966
they give you a little liquidity

152
00:03:48,133 --> 00:03:49,900
so one place going dark

153
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:51,166
doesn't shut down your whole life

154
00:03:51,300 --> 00:03:52,866
what's most moving about Su Dongpo

155
00:03:52,866 --> 00:03:54,000
is this ability

156
00:03:54,133 --> 00:03:55,400
of course he wanted to do things

157
00:03:55,433 --> 00:03:56,500
to be understood

158
00:03:56,533 --> 00:03:58,233
to be back in a better place

159
00:03:58,333 --> 00:04:00,200
but when these were gone for a while

160
00:04:00,366 --> 00:04:02,600
he wouldn't let life go blank

161
00:04:02,766 --> 00:04:04,533
he would take whatever was in front of him

162
00:04:04,533 --> 00:04:05,866
and turn it back into life

163
00:04:05,933 --> 00:04:06,733
a meal

164
00:04:06,733 --> 00:04:07,533
a river

165
00:04:07,533 --> 00:04:08,300
a friend

166
00:04:08,366 --> 00:04:09,200
a poem

167
00:04:09,233 --> 00:04:10,166
a joke

168
00:04:10,233 --> 00:04:11,600
none of these are escape

169
00:04:11,733 --> 00:04:13,833
they are small supports inside a hard situation

170
00:04:14,066 --> 00:04:16,000
modern people easily look down on these

171
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:17,466
what's the point of walking

172
00:04:17,466 --> 00:04:18,633
what's the point of cooking

173
00:04:18,666 --> 00:04:20,100
what's the point of writing a few lines

174
00:04:20,233 --> 00:04:21,600
but when you're truly in trouble

175
00:04:21,733 --> 00:04:23,700
these small things are what catch you

176
00:04:23,766 --> 00:04:26,000
not every value has to cash out at once

177
00:04:26,066 --> 00:04:26,833
some value

178
00:04:26,833 --> 00:04:28,866
is what keeps you from shattering in the worst moment

179
00:04:28,966 --> 00:04:31,233
this is also why many people get more fragile the busier they get

180
00:04:31,333 --> 00:04:34,166
because they trade every hour for outside results

181
00:04:34,166 --> 00:04:36,300
without saving any inner supports for themselves

182
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:37,200
work stops

183
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:38,000
the person goes empty

184
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:38,933
a relationship breaks

185
00:04:38,933 --> 00:04:39,733
they cave in

186
00:04:39,866 --> 00:04:40,700
metrics dip

187
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:41,800
they doubt themselves

188
00:04:42,033 --> 00:04:44,433
if someone lives only on outside applause

189
00:04:44,466 --> 00:04:45,500
the moment it goes quiet

190
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,366
they hear a huge hollow inside

191
00:04:47,533 --> 00:04:49,000
what Su Dongpo reminds us of

192
00:04:49,033 --> 00:04:50,900
isn't to pretend nothing matters

193
00:04:50,966 --> 00:04:52,300
but to not let your heart

194
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:53,600
run on a single outlet

195
00:04:54,066 --> 00:04:56,400
so how should an ordinary person use this idea

196
00:04:56,533 --> 00:04:57,266
first

197
00:04:57,266 --> 00:04:58,666
list your identities

198
00:04:58,700 --> 00:04:59,900
don't just write your job

199
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:00,766
write friend too

200
00:05:00,933 --> 00:05:02,100
write parent to a child

201
00:05:02,100 --> 00:05:03,433
someone who likes to cook

202
00:05:03,533 --> 00:05:04,833
someone who can write

203
00:05:04,866 --> 00:05:06,200
someone who can fix things

204
00:05:06,233 --> 00:05:07,466
someone willing to move

205
00:05:07,533 --> 00:05:09,066
someone who can be alone

206
00:05:09,266 --> 00:05:10,100
the more you write

207
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:12,100
the more you realize you're not one seat

208
00:05:12,233 --> 00:05:12,933
second

209
00:05:12,933 --> 00:05:15,400
keep a few supports that don't depend on approval

210
00:05:15,466 --> 00:05:16,366
a hobby

211
00:05:16,366 --> 00:05:18,100
don't immediately try to monetize it

212
00:05:18,233 --> 00:05:19,033
a friend

213
00:05:19,233 --> 00:05:21,200
you don't have to look put together around

214
00:05:21,333 --> 00:05:22,200
a skill

215
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:22,966
build it slowly

216
00:05:22,966 --> 00:05:24,766
without posting it daily to prove anything

217
00:05:24,933 --> 00:05:26,166
a cheap kind of joy

218
00:05:26,166 --> 00:05:27,633
so when money is tight

219
00:05:27,666 --> 00:05:29,233
you still have some taste in your days

220
00:05:29,333 --> 00:05:30,533
the more of these you have

221
00:05:30,533 --> 00:05:32,666
the less any single failure can take you down

222
00:05:32,833 --> 00:05:33,533
third

223
00:05:33,533 --> 00:05:34,633
when you hit a low

224
00:05:34,666 --> 00:05:36,433
don't rush to ask if you're done for

225
00:05:36,433 --> 00:05:37,133
first ask

226
00:05:37,133 --> 00:05:38,700
which of my supports are still standing

227
00:05:38,766 --> 00:05:39,966
what can I still write

228
00:05:39,966 --> 00:05:40,966
who can I still see

229
00:05:41,033 --> 00:05:42,366
what meal can I still cook

230
00:05:42,466 --> 00:05:43,700
what road can I still walk

231
00:05:43,766 --> 00:05:45,466
what small thing can I still do well

232
00:05:45,533 --> 00:05:46,766
these questions are small

233
00:05:46,766 --> 00:05:49,233
but they pull you back from total defeat

234
00:05:49,300 --> 00:05:50,100
a lot of times

235
00:05:50,266 --> 00:05:52,366
people don't stand back up in one move

236
00:05:52,366 --> 00:05:53,766
it's small thing by small thing

237
00:05:53,766 --> 00:05:55,600
slowly bringing the feel of life back

238
00:05:55,666 --> 00:05:57,266
Su Dongpo was demoted that many times

239
00:05:57,300 --> 00:05:58,466
he didn't win every round

240
00:05:58,533 --> 00:06:00,233
but he was never left with only the loss

241
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:01,566
that is his real strength

242
00:06:01,566 --> 00:06:02,733
he shows us

243
00:06:02,733 --> 00:06:04,966
a person doesn't have to be defined by one identity

244
00:06:04,966 --> 00:06:06,600
and doesn't have to turn one setback

245
00:06:06,633 --> 00:06:08,400
into a verdict on the whole life

246
00:06:08,533 --> 00:06:09,533
true openness

247
00:06:09,533 --> 00:06:11,166
isn't telling yourself it doesn't matter

248
00:06:11,266 --> 00:06:13,066
it's that you actually have other connections

249
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:14,300
to friends

250
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:15,533
to food

251
00:06:15,533 --> 00:06:16,733
to writing

252
00:06:16,733 --> 00:06:17,966
to body

253
00:06:17,966 --> 00:06:19,233
to the world

254
00:06:19,266 --> 00:06:20,433
the more of these

255
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:22,600
the harder it is for fate to wipe you clean in one push

256
00:06:22,766 --> 00:06:25,166
so Su Dongpo's reminder for ordinary people

257
00:06:25,166 --> 00:06:26,500
isn't to be optimistic

258
00:06:26,566 --> 00:06:28,166
it's to not let life run on one axis

259
00:06:28,166 --> 00:06:29,400
don't lean only on a job title

260
00:06:29,433 --> 00:06:30,766
don't lean only on one result

261
00:06:30,766 --> 00:06:32,433
don't lean only on one line of approval

262
00:06:32,466 --> 00:06:34,000
someone with many supports

263
00:06:34,033 --> 00:06:35,400
even when banished far away

264
00:06:35,433 --> 00:06:36,866
can still at some dusk

265
00:06:36,866 --> 00:06:37,933
light a fire

266
00:06:37,933 --> 00:06:38,966
cook a meal

267
00:06:39,066 --> 00:06:40,566
and slowly find himself back

268
00:06:40,566 --> 00:06:42,366
there's another point easy to miss

269
00:06:42,366 --> 00:06:43,966
supports don't have to be high-level

270
00:06:44,033 --> 00:06:45,733
when people talk about rebuilding life

271
00:06:45,733 --> 00:06:46,800
they think big

272
00:06:46,833 --> 00:06:48,400
I'm going to redesign my life

273
00:06:48,433 --> 00:06:49,533
find my passion

274
00:06:49,533 --> 00:06:51,266
become a better self right now

275
00:06:51,466 --> 00:06:52,866
these are nice ideas

276
00:06:52,866 --> 00:06:54,100
but when you're low

277
00:06:54,133 --> 00:06:55,666
you usually don't have that much energy

278
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:57,133
what really helps then

279
00:06:57,133 --> 00:06:58,600
is small supports

280
00:06:58,633 --> 00:07:00,066
today eat one good meal

281
00:07:00,133 --> 00:07:01,800
tomorrow walk for twenty minutes

282
00:07:01,833 --> 00:07:03,566
message an old friend

283
00:07:03,566 --> 00:07:05,900
clear one small clean corner of the room

284
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:07,533
write down the mess in your head

285
00:07:07,533 --> 00:07:09,366
these don't feel like big things

286
00:07:09,366 --> 00:07:10,966
but they slowly remind you

287
00:07:10,966 --> 00:07:12,133
I'm still inside life

288
00:07:12,133 --> 00:07:14,066
failure hasn't taken all of me

289
00:07:14,066 --> 00:07:15,866
a lot of what's moving about Su Dongpo

290
00:07:15,866 --> 00:07:17,200
is in these small places

291
00:07:17,233 --> 00:07:18,600
not always grand

292
00:07:18,633 --> 00:07:19,966
not always vast

293
00:07:19,966 --> 00:07:21,600
but when the days had narrowed

294
00:07:21,700 --> 00:07:23,133
he could still from a bite of food

295
00:07:23,133 --> 00:07:24,066
a patch of scenery

296
00:07:24,066 --> 00:07:25,100
a few lines of writing

297
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:26,433
keep one breath for himself

298
00:07:26,466 --> 00:07:28,700
ordinary people don't need to push themselves to be Su Dongpo

299
00:07:28,833 --> 00:07:31,166
you don't have to write a masterpiece after every setback

300
00:07:31,266 --> 00:07:33,666
or turn every low point into a growth story

301
00:07:33,666 --> 00:07:35,533
you just need to hold a few small supports

302
00:07:35,533 --> 00:07:37,800
so one event doesn't fully drown you

303
00:07:37,833 --> 00:07:38,633
a lot of times

304
00:07:38,733 --> 00:07:40,566
people don't survive on big principles

305
00:07:40,566 --> 00:07:41,766
but on a hot meal

306
00:07:41,766 --> 00:07:42,733
one walk

307
00:07:42,733 --> 00:07:44,200
one line saying someone still thinks of you

308
00:07:44,233 --> 00:07:46,233
a small sense of I can still do something

309
00:07:46,266 --> 00:07:47,166
these are small

310
00:07:47,166 --> 00:07:48,000
but steady

311
00:07:48,066 --> 00:07:49,600
so don't think of resilience

312
00:07:49,633 --> 00:07:50,833
as just white-knuckling

313
00:07:50,866 --> 00:07:52,433
white-knuckling holds for a while

314
00:07:52,466 --> 00:07:54,566
but no one can live on grit alone

315
00:07:54,566 --> 00:07:56,000
resilience that lasts

316
00:07:56,033 --> 00:07:57,866
is more like laying down cushions for yourself

317
00:07:57,866 --> 00:07:58,966
when work is stuck

318
00:07:58,966 --> 00:07:59,900
there's still body

319
00:07:59,966 --> 00:08:00,966
when relationships knot

320
00:08:00,966 --> 00:08:01,900
there's still work

321
00:08:01,933 --> 00:08:03,033
when metrics dip

322
00:08:03,066 --> 00:08:03,966
there's still life

323
00:08:03,966 --> 00:08:05,666
when one identity dims

324
00:08:05,666 --> 00:08:07,366
another still glows a little

325
00:08:07,366 --> 00:08:08,433
this isn't distraction

326
00:08:08,466 --> 00:08:10,866
it's not giving fate a one-key delete on you

327
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:12,966
many people concentrate their life too much

328
00:08:12,966 --> 00:08:14,200
concentration is efficient

329
00:08:14,233 --> 00:08:15,133
and also dangerous

330
00:08:15,133 --> 00:08:17,033
because once the single pillar cracks

331
00:08:17,166 --> 00:08:18,766
the whole person has nowhere to stand

332
00:08:18,766 --> 00:08:20,366
Su Dongpo's reminder to us

333
00:08:20,366 --> 00:08:22,033
is before things go wrong

334
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:23,333
plant a few more trees

335
00:08:23,333 --> 00:08:24,433
so when the wind comes

336
00:08:24,466 --> 00:08:26,400
you aren't clinging to a single branch

337
00:08:26,433 --> 00:08:28,300
the earlier you add supports to your life

338
00:08:28,300 --> 00:08:29,666
the less you panic in lows

339
00:08:29,700 --> 00:08:31,166
don't wait until you lose a job

340
00:08:31,166 --> 00:08:32,866
to realize you had no hobby

341
00:08:32,866 --> 00:08:34,366
don't wait until a relationship breaks

342
00:08:34,366 --> 00:08:35,900
to find you had no friends

343
00:08:36,033 --> 00:08:37,566
don't wait until traffic drops

344
00:08:37,633 --> 00:08:40,233
to admit you left nothing but results behind

345
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:42,100
next episode we talk about Naval

346
00:08:42,133 --> 00:08:44,433
many people think what ordinary people lack is effort

347
00:08:44,466 --> 00:08:46,000
but what really widens the gap

348
00:08:46,033 --> 00:08:49,333
may be whether you've turned effort into reusable leverage
